{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfmL7nBGbc9CJm8dCd4JR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RrkkQsRYLmWYsoqTrzrzZX","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop; D=iter_4/candidate_0\ncat > $D/hypothesis.md << 'EOF'\nPeople's picture of a fair coin keeps a running tally of how far heads lead tails as they read a sequence, and they believe chance corrects that lead: whenever one face is ahead, they expect the next flip to favour the face that is behind, the more strongly the bigger the current lead. A sequence therefore looks random when its tally drifts and is promptly pulled back towards balance, and non-random when a lead keeps growing before it is corrected — so the path to the final count matters, and breaking a long streak (which corrects a large lead) makes a sequence look much more random. This self-correcting chance coin is weighed against the regular generators people suspect (a switch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips) exactly as in the current best account, and replaces its run-length gambler's belief.\nEOF\necho tally_correcting_chance_coin > $D/model_name.txt\npython3 - << 'EOF'\nsrc=open('models/streak_weary_chance_pseudoflip.py').read()\nbody=src[src.index('import math'):]\ndoc='''\"\"\"Tally-correcting chance coin weighed against the regular generators.\n\nPeople's picture of a fair coin keeps a running tally of heads minus tails and\nexpects chance to correct the lead: whenever one face is ahead by |D| flips,\nthe believed log-odds that the next flip favours the trailing face rise by a\nshared fitted r per unit of lead. Each flip read while the tally is unbalanced\ncontributes (r / 2) * |D| * (+1 if it lands on the trailing face, -1 if it\nextends the lead) to the chance log-likelihood, so a sequence whose tally\ndrifts and is promptly corrected looks random, a growing lead looks non-random,\nand breaking a long streak (correcting a large lead) is strongly rewarded: the\npath to the final count matters, not the count. Everything else is the current\nbest account (`streak_weary_chance_pseudoflip`): person-specific believed switch\nrate and a second-order switch belief in the chance coin, weighed against a\nswitch-biased coin, a heads-favoured trick coin and a repeating motif with slips\n(person-specific motif suspicion), per-flip evidence with pseudo-flip dilution,\nheavy-tailed signed person sensitivity and a side habit. The tally correction\nreplaces that model's run-length gambler's belief.\n\"\"\"\n\n'''\nbody=body.replace('''    gam = 0.0\n    run = 1\n    for x, y in zip(seq, seq[1:]):\n        if run >= 3:\n            gam += (run - 2) * (1.0 if x != y else -1.0)\n        run = 1 if x != y else run + 1\n''','''    # Running tally: each flip read while one face leads by |D| scores\n    # +|D| if it lands on the trailing face, -|D| if it extends the lead.\n    gam = 0.0\n    lead = 0\n    for x in seq:\n        step = 1 if x == \"H\" else -1\n        if lead != 0:\n            gam += abs(lead) * (1.0 if step * lead < 0 else -1.0)\n        lead += step\n''')\nbody=body.replace('''    # Gambler's run-length belief: shared rise g in the believed log-odds of\n    # switching per flip the current run lasts beyond two (g > 0: long streaks\n    # are improbable under chance beyond their switch count).\n    g_run = pm.Normal(\"g_run\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.3)''','''    # Tally-correcting chance coin: shared rise r in the believed log-odds that\n    # the next flip favours the trailing face, per unit of current lead.\n    g_run = pm.Normal(\"r_tally\", mu=0.0, sigma=0.3)''')\nopen('iter_4/candidate_0/candidate.py','w').write(doc+body)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"lead\\|r_tally\" $D/candidate.py | head\ncd /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/runs/run3/repo && /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/venv/bin/python -m src.pipelines.inner_loop.check_candidate --candidate-dir /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/iter_4/candidate_0 --responses /scratch/users/kushinm/auto-psych/outer_loop_live/run3/data/subjective_randomness/experiment3/model_loop/responses.csv 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8166,"cache_read_input_tokens":81828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8166,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fab817f-3631-4404-ba09-4da243a6cc2f","uuid":"17be78ac-e475-403e-bc6e-543058e1fc9f","timestamp":"2026-10-06T16:52:36.649Z","request_id":"req_011CfmL7mmiVp3Lr4AVotbST"}
